-// Linux can still report mandatory error or hangup conditions for a zero-interest
-// epoll entry; Darwin has no filter to report while its mask is zero.
-// On Darwin, a failed multi-filter update is rolled back to the prior mask when
-// possible; if rollback also fails, the poller retains the exact known native
-// mask so a later ModifyFD or UnregisterFD can clean it up.
